{ignore}
<p><code>{cannot}</code> is <a href="?tag/can">{can}</a> turned round: the content renders
when the gate answers no, and the part after its own <code>{else}</code> - or the
<code>&#64;else&#64;</code> half - when it answers yes. Everything else is the same: the first item is
the ability, the others what the gate is given, an enclosing loop's name its current row.</p>

<p>A guest is refused by every gate that does not take NULL for its user, so for a guest
<code>{cannot}</code> renders its content for those. An ability nobody defined counts as no -
and is an error under the strict check, as with <code>{can}</code>.</p>
{/ignore}
